WEBVTT

00:00:09,390 --> 00:00:15,150
So, now I'm done with the mastectomy and the reconstructive surgeries.

00:00:15,150 --> 00:00:18,990
I want to focus on making sure that there's no reoccurrence.

00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:21,750
In what order do I complete these?

00:00:21,750 --> 00:00:29,390
Order a complete wellness panel, order cheek swab testing, do a one-on-one consult with you.

00:00:29,390 --> 00:00:33,190
I would do it in probably the stack order that you wrote that.

00:00:33,190 --> 00:00:36,230
I would get this going right away.

00:00:36,230 --> 00:00:38,790
Order this, get this blood test done.

00:00:38,790 --> 00:00:42,390
We tell you you can send in the cheek swab sample right away.

00:00:42,390 --> 00:00:48,150
And then after we do the cheek swab testing, unless there's things that you want to discuss

00:00:48,150 --> 00:00:55,750
before we tested, put a new protocol together for you, you could wait and tell you get

00:00:55,750 --> 00:01:00,030
that protocol back from me and then schedule the one-on-one.

00:01:00,030 --> 00:01:06,030
So it really has to do with the purpose of this one-on-one if you want to talk about it

00:01:06,030 --> 00:01:07,030
before.

00:01:07,030 --> 00:01:13,270
Some people are like, I really want to change my whole protocol, cut my back or maybe

00:01:13,270 --> 00:01:16,950
have financial concerns or maybe they just want to change your life.

00:01:16,950 --> 00:01:22,230
They don't want to take as many supplements anymore or whatever it is that I can be a little

00:01:22,230 --> 00:01:24,230
bit more choosy.

00:01:24,230 --> 00:01:30,430
But of course you could write that on any specifics on your cheek swab testing form, or we

00:01:30,430 --> 00:01:31,430
didn't know that too.

00:01:31,430 --> 00:01:36,750
And then wait until you get that back and tell you might formulate some more questions to

00:01:36,750 --> 00:01:37,750
do on one-on-one consult.

00:01:37,750 --> 00:01:45,590
And remember, you could just schedule that yourself right on that page on the member site

00:01:45,590 --> 00:01:51,150
or on our self-scheduling page on our regular website as well.

